[agent] First, I will create a Python script to:
[agent] 1. Read the CSV from the volume.
[agent] 2. Create a table in the Unity Catalog.
[agent] 3. Detect the distribution shift using statistical methods.
[agent:write] ?
[agent:result] path: /Users/wolffbe/workspace/banter/testbed/results/20_db-full-cli-sdk-skills-mistral-large/mistral-large-3/databricks/cli/1.3.0/no-skills/ops/prediction_monitoring/1/task/create_table_and_detect_shift.py
[agent:result] bytes_written: 1438
[agent:result] content: from pyspark.sql import SparkSession
[agent:result] from pyspark.sql.functions import col, to_timestamp
[agent:result] from pyspark.sql.types import DoubleType
[agent:result] import pandas as pd
[agent:result] from scipy.stats import ks_2samp
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] # Initialize Spark
[agent:result] spark = SparkSession.builder.getOrCreate()
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] # Read the CSV from the volume
[agent:result] df = spark.read.format("csv").option("header", "true").option("inferSchema", "true").load("dbfs:/Volumes/workspace/mlpabbc4768/mlpabbc4768_volume/prediction_log.csv")
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] # Convert ts to timestamp and prediction to double
[agent:result] df = df.withColumn("ts", to_timestamp(col("ts"))).withColumn("prediction", col("prediction").cast(DoubleType()))
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] # Write to Unity Catalog
[agent:result] df.write.saveAsTable("workspace.mlpabbc4768.mlpabbc4768_prediction_log")
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] # Convert to Pandas for analysis
[agent:result] pdf = df.select("ts", "prediction").toPandas()
[agent:result] pdf = pdf.sort_values("ts")
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] # Detect shift using Kolmogorov-Smirnov test
[agent:result] window_size = 150  # ~1 day of data
[agent:result] shift_date = None
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] for i in range(window_size, len(pdf), window_size):
[agent:result]     before = pdf.iloc[i-window_size:i]["prediction"]
[agent:result]     after = pdf.iloc[i:i+window_size]["prediction"]
[agent:result]     ks_stat, p_value = ks_2samp(before, after)
[agent:result]     if p_value < 0.01:  # Significant shift
[agent:result]         shift_date = pdf.iloc[i]["ts"].strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
[agent:result]         break
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] # Write the result to submission/answers.json
[agent:result] import json
[agent:result] import os
[agent:result] os.makedirs("submission", exist_ok=True)
[agent:result] with open("submission/answers.json", "w") as f:
[agent:result]     json.dump({"onset": shift_date}, f)
